 ## Overview
-Custom Shading Models provide a framework for defining arbitrary illumination calculations within volume rendering and ray-marching pipelines, allowing developers to replace standard analytic lighting with user-defined logic. This family enables the implementation of specialized effects such as physically based microfacet reflections, directional occlusion, and color-space-specific glow, which are not covered by generic diffuse or specular models. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Distance Color Blending](791-distance-color-blending.md) by operating on explicit geometric data (normals, positions) rather than raw scalar field values, and from [Ambient Occlusion via SDF](1631-ambient-occlusion-via-sdf.md) by allowing full directional light integration rather than just ambient darkening.
