 ### [Single-Atomic High-Quality Robust Variant (HQS1R)](10218-single-atomic-high-quality-robust-variant-hqs1r.md)
-HQS1R is a high-quality point cloud rendering method that reduces aliasing by blending overlapping points together, similar to mipmapping. It is a simplified, compute-based implementation of the blending algorithm from [BHZK05], designed to be faster than aliased `GL_POINTS` results while providing anti-aliasing. Unlike surface splatting [ZPVG01], it blends overlapping points without considering oriented disks with variable radii. It sets itself apart from the [Single-Atomic High-Quality Variant (HQS1x)](#single-atomic-high-quality-variant-hqs1x) by using a robust overflow protection mechanism that prevents artifacts when more than 255 points contribute to a pixel.
