 ## Background
-The concept of custom shading in volume rendering originated with early libraries like VolPack, which introduced the `vpSetCallback` mechanism allowing users to define per-voxel shading routines instead of relying on fixed lookup tables [S1]. This allowed for arbitrary color transfer functions and lighting models but noted potential performance degradation [S1]. Modern implementations have expanded this to include physically based rendering (PBR) models like GGX [S1][S2, unofficial], specialized techniques for point clouds like HQS1R [S1], and color-space specific methods like YUV shading [S1]. The family also encompasses discrete voxel-specific pipelines [17027-voxel-specific-shading-pipelines.md] and procedural surface shaders for specific domains like road rendering [S2, unofficial].
